{% from "icon/macro.njk" import icon %}

{# The one thing on this page that needs a line of script, and it earns it: an
   operator's whole job here is to carry an id or a reference somewhere else —
   into a log query, into a ticket, into Slack — and selecting eight characters
   of truncated mono out of a dense row with a mouse is a fiddle they were
   doing twenty times an hour.

   Progressive by construction. The button ships `disabled`, because a button
   that looks live and does nothing when clicked is worse than no button: with
   scripting off, or before the module has run, it is visibly inert rather
   than a broken promise. `do-copy-button` enables it on upgrade, and only when
   the clipboard API is actually there to enable it for.

   Invisible until the row is under the pointer (or the button itself is
   tabbed to): one of these on every id and every reference, drawn at all
   times, would put forty icons on a twenty-row page and the page would be
   about its buttons. `group-hover` needs the `group` class on the row cell,
   which views/events.njk puts there.

   `always` turns that off. A page about one event has five of these, not
   forty, and each sits beside a value the operator came to the page to carry
   somewhere else — a button they have to find by hovering is a button they do
   not know is there. It is still held back to 70% until it is pointed at, so
   five of them read as affordances beside the values rather than as five
   icons of their own.

   The label carries the noun — `Copy event id` — because "Copy" alone, said
   forty times down a page, names nothing for a screen reader walking the row.

   Both glyphs are in the markup and CSS swaps them (client/dev-ops.css): the
   check has to replace the clipboard for a second and a half without the
   button changing size, and a swap the element does by rewriting innerHTML
   would throw the row's layout for a frame. #}
<do-copy-button class="inline-flex shrink-0 align-middle" value="{{ params.value }}" data-testid="do-copy-button">
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-ghost btn-xs do-copy-button h-4 min-h-0 w-4 rounded-sm p-0 {{ "opacity-70 hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100" if params.always else "opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 focus-visible:opacity-100" }}" aria-label="Copy {{ params.what }}" disabled data-testid="do-copy-button-control">
    {{ icon({ name: 'clipboard', class: 'do-copy-idle h-3 w-3' }) }}
    {{ icon({ name: 'check', class: 'do-copy-done h-3 w-3' }) }}
  </button>
</do-copy-button>
